{{/*
  cleanup-child-conversations — the standard block emitted by prompts that spawn
  child conversations, telling the agent to reap the finished ones before the
  `_shared/offer-delete-conversation` final step runs.

  This matters because self-destructing cascade-deletes the children implicitly:
  without an explicit reap, a child that is still working is torn down without
  a chance to report. The "leave still-working children alone" clause is the
  safety invariant that must stay identical across callers.

  Usage — immediately before the final self-delete step:

      {{ template "_shared/cleanup-child-conversations" . }}
*/}}
Clean up any child conversations that reported back and are no longer needed with
`mitto_conversation_delete_mitto(self_id: "{{ .Session.ID }}", conversation_id: "<child-id>")`.
Leave any child that is still working, or that you did not spawn, untouched.

A child that is idle without a report is unresolved, not finished: check `mitto_conversation_get`,
read `mitto_conversation_history` (its last messages may already hold the report — never claim it
never reported without reading them), then `mitto_conversation_send_prompt` a concrete query and
`mitto_children_tasks_wait` it; act on the answer. Never defer on `agent_idle`/timeout alone.
